@startuml dawg-minimization
' ============================================================================
' DAWG minimization via 64-bit signature hashing (FxHash).
' Source of truth: src/node_signature.rs (NodeSignature::compute) and
' src/dynamic_dawg/core.rs (compute_signatures_dfs / minimize_incremental /
' nodes_structurally_equal).
'
' The algorithm is bottom-up (post-order DFS = deepest-first). Each node folds a
' 64-bit signature  FxHash(is_final, sorted[(label, child_signature)]).  Nodes
' that hash equal are MERGE CANDIDATES; because a 64-bit hash can collide
' (birthday paradox), the equal-signature branch is guarded by an explicit
' structural-equality check before the parent edge is redirected and the new
' node discarded.
'
' LAYOUT: a top decision (classify by signature) followed by a VERTICAL STACK of
' the four disjoint outcome cases (condition -> action -> rationale, one colored
' card each), so the figure reads top-to-bottom and stays within the prose
' column. The amber container preserves the original 'collision guard' grouping:
' it wraps CASE 1 (merge) and CASE 2 (collision) — the two cases reached only
' once a live equal-signature candidate exists.
'
' Color key (mirrors docs/diagrams/README.md house style):
'   green  #C8E6C9 = signature computation (the bottom-up fold, in-memory)
'   blue   #BBDEFB = the registry / canonical-table lookup + decision
'   amber  #FFF59D = the collision guard (structural equality) — the safety net
'   red    #FFCDD2 = collision detected -> do NOT merge (register as distinct)
'   neutral #ECEFF1 = terminal / edge-rewrite bookkeeping
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 280
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}
skinparam card {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontName "DejaVu Sans"
}

title DAWG minimization — signature hashing with a 64-bit-collision guard

card "minimize()  ▶\nreach a near-minimal DAWG" as START #C8E6C9

rectangle "**① Signature fold** (post-order DFS)\nchildren first ⇒ deepest\nnode finalizes first" as P1a #C8E6C9
rectangle "Fold each node's signature\n`sig = FxHash(is_final,`\n`sorted[(label, child_sig)])`\n(sorted ⇒ order-independent)" as P1b #C8E6C9

rectangle "**② Classify nodes** (leaves-first)\ntake next node + its `sig`; probe\nthe canonical table; scan the\nbucket's **live** canonicals — skip\nmerged (`node_mapping[c] == c`).\nFour disjoint outcomes ↓" as CLASSIFY #BBDEFB

rectangle "**Collision guard** — structural-eq" as GUARD #FFF59D {
  card "**CASE 1 · MERGE**\n--\n**when:** `structurally_equal` —\nsame is_final · labels ·\nchild canonicals\n**do:** redirect parent edge to\ncanonical; `node_mapping[node]`\n`= canonical`; drop duplicate\n**why:** right langs identical —\nsame accept flag + same\n(label→canonical) edges;\nthe space win" as C1 #C8E6C9
  card "**CASE 2 · HASH COLLISION**\n**— keep distinct**\n--\n**when:** equal `sig`,\n**diff structure** (birthday\nparadox)\n**do:** do NOT merge; register\na //new// canonical in the bucket\n**why:** else a birthday collision\nfuses two right langs and\ncorrupts the DAWG" as C2 #FFCDD2
}

card "**CASE 3 · APPEND**\n--\n**when:** `sig` in table, but\n**no live** equal-`sig`\ncanonical (all bucket entries\nmerged or differ)\n**do:** append node as a new\ncanonical in the bucket" as C3 #BBDEFB

card "**CASE 4 · FRESH bucket**\n--\n**when:** `sig` ∉ canonical table\n(first time this `sig` is seen)\n**do:** fresh bucket\n`sig → [node]`; mark it canonical" as C4 #BBDEFB

rectangle "**③ Rewrite & compact**\nredirect **every** edge target\nthrough `node_mapping`" as P3a #ECEFF1
rectangle "drop nodes unreachable from\nthe root (`find_reachable_nodes`)" as P3b #ECEFF1
rectangle "clear suffix cache;\nrecompute ref-counts" as P3c #ECEFF1

card "▧ minimized, compacted DAWG" as DONE #ECEFF1

START --> P1a
P1a --> P1b
P1b --> CLASSIFY
CLASSIFY --> C1 : live equal-`sig`\ncandidate\n⇒ guard
C1 --> C2 : else ·\nhash collision
C2 --> C3 : else ·\nno live\nequal-`sig`
C3 --> C4 : else ·\n`sig` ∉ table
C4 --> P3a
P3a --> P3b
P3b --> P3c
P3c --> DONE

legend right
| Color | Stage |
|<#C8E6C9>| signature fold (bottom-up) |
|<#BBDEFB>| canonical-table lookup |
|<#FFF59D>| structural-equality guard |
|<#FFCDD2>| 64-bit collision → keep distinct |
|<#ECEFF1>| edge rewrite + compaction |
endlegend
@enduml
